6. Important points for your lab exam
insert() – Inserts elements into the BST.

inorder() – Displays elements in ascending order.

leafcount() – Counts nodes having no children.

nonleafcount() – Counts nodes having at least one child.

root – Points to the root node of the tree.

Most importantly: You do not need to use n/2 for counting. The two recursive functions work for any shape of Binary Search Tree.








